e has been hailed a hero and could  likely testify in the trial ranking was  previously deemed incompetent to stand  trial and was treated for schizophrenia  jury selection which started tuesday has  been a difficult task given the media  coverage of the case opening statements  are set to begin on monday  legal analyst kirk nermey and co-host  terry austin join us again to break down  the waffle house shooting  terry i respect james shaw jr's opinion  i totally get it but to me he's a hero  so  how do you think having a hero testify  against a defendant will play out for  ranking  ryan there's no question that the jury  is going to be very sympathetic i mean  this man risked his life and he could  have easily been killed and i think it's  the testimony that the jury is going to  really admire they're going to respect  it they're going to have sympathy and  when you compare that to the actual  defendant who kills someone i think the  jury is definitely going to lean in  favor obviously of making this  individual guilty absolutely now kirk  bizarre facts are likely to come out of  this case as you saw um shaw jr had his  hand wrapped there because the barrel of  the gun was so hot it burned his hand  and ranking was naked but for the jacket  he had on top of him how will these  facts play into the case  well i think ultimately you know because  mr ranking might be using some mental  health defense he's been treated for  schizophrenia some of those bizarre  facts could at least give the jury  insight into that the validity of that  but i think ultimately you know this is  what we would call in the criminal  defense business a long-form guilty plea  because we have so many witnesses  against him we have mr shaw jr who  stopped a potentially even more horrific  scene and i think the horrific nature of  this crime the extent of it the extent  of what could happen is what the jury is  going to be fixated on and ultimately no  matter how long this long form guilty  plea ta